    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d909">

                <pb facs="1170" n="1158" xml:id="pg1158"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.61/9–1745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-02T20:00:00-05:00">November 2, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2271. UrAir 231, September 17. Navy Secretary Forrestal has requested Dept to
                    make strong representations to Soviet Govt with regard to case of Mrs. V. I.
                        Tolley.<anchor n="75" xml:id="d909-f1"/> Unless you feel that the case would
                    be prejudiced by such action you are again requested to take up with the
                    SovFonOff.</p>
                <p>Was Mrs. Tolley among those given oral understanding? Please inform Dept which
                    persons given oral understanding.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d909-f1" n="75" xml:id="d909-f1-content">
                <p>Vladilena Isayevna Tolley (Mrs. Kemp Tolley).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
